  "authoring_instructions": "main-v2 EXACT PROMPT:\nCorrect the SECOND attached newly generated64-pose tiger atlas using the FIRST attached unchanged original tiger portrait. The only semantic defect is that the FIFTH column (W) wrongly faces RIGHT. Repaint all EIGHT poses in the FIFTH column as a genuine TRUE LEFT-FACING PROFILE: head and long saber teeth on the LEFT, tail and rump on the RIGHT, all walking and attack contacts directed LEFT. Do not reuse the current right-facing W poses. Retain the other seven correctly oriented columns and their genuine phases/identity/body volume, keeping the full64-pose8columns×8rows layout, fully transparent RGBA background, huge transparent gutters and intact complete tails/paws. First-column E stays RIGHT; secondSE front-right; thirdS fullFRONT down; fourthSW front-left; FIFTHW TRUELEFT; sixthNW rear-left; seventhN fullBACK up; eighthNE rear-right. No labels/grid/background. Rows2idle/3walk/3attack exactly as provided; maintain clean separated frame rectangles. Do not flip the complete sheet or exchange N/S. Preserve the actual WHITE saber-toothed tiger with dense narrow BLACK stripes, heavy white shoulder ruff/mane, round feline ears, pale feline face, very long paired ivory upper canine fangs, four muscular striped legs with broad white paws, long striped feline tail. Keep exact original proportions and stripe palette; never change to orange, lion or humanoid. N shows rump/striped back and rear of mane/head, with face/fangs hidden. S shows original face and both long fangs. Walking has three different alternating four-paw contact phases. Attack draws the neck/forequarters back, lunges the original saber-fanged muzzle and one natural paw in the compass direction, then returns.\n\nhit-v3 EXACT PROMPT:\nEdit the SECOND attached newly drawn tiger atlas only to provide much larger TRANSPARENT GUTTERS. The FIRST image is the unchanged original identity reference. Keep exactly the SAME32 real poses arranged EIGHT direction COLUMNS